# teademo: Tea program + TextInput widget under a real pty.
# Frame trace (each repaint is ONE write: \e[1A move-up + \e[2K + value +
# \e[7m \e[0m block cursor + \r\n; first paint hides the cursor):
#   init    \e[?25l \e[2K\e[7m \e[0m\r\n
#   'h'     \e[1A\e[2Kh\e[7m \e[0m\r\n
#   'i'     \e[1A\e[2Khi\e[7m \e[0m\r\n
#   \e[A    \e[1A\e[2Khi\e[7m \e[0m\r\n   (ignored key -> same-content repaint)
#   0x7F    \e[1A\e[2Kh\e[7m \e[0m\r\n
#   \r      \e[?25h + exit 0
# Frames are self-similar, so each needle spans a frame BOUNDARY (previous
# frame's tail -> new frame's head) — such a substring cannot exist until the
# new frame is actually written, making every expect deterministic.
expect \e[?25l
send hi
expect hi\e[7m
send \e[A
expect hi\e[7m \e[0m\r\n\e[1A\e[2Khi
send \x7f
expect hi\e[7m \e[0m\r\n\e[1A\e[2Kh\e[7m
send \r
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
